/*
 * Declares the RangeContainsValue class.
 *
 * RangeContainsValue represents the binary containment operator for ranges.
 * It models expressions of the form:
 *
 *     value in range
 *
 * Unlike purely compile-time binary operators, this operator always relies on a
 * runtime function call to determine whether the left operand is contained in
 * the right operand. The right operand must be a range type, and the operator
 * produces a boolean result.
 *
 * <hr>
 *
 * @Package: ymirc
 * @Module: ymirc::semantic::generator::value::operator::binary::range
 * @File: ymirc/semantic/generator/value/operator/binary/range.yr
 * @Author(s):
 *   - Emile Cadorel <ecadorel@gmail.com>
 *
 * @Created(YYYY-MM-DD): 2023-11-10
 * @Copyright(C) 2021–2026 GNU-Ymir
 * @License
 *   ```text
